! Topic–comment organization

Mandarin often puts the item being discussed first, then makes a comment about it.

* 我喜欢这本书。 — Wǒ xǐhuan zhè běn shū. — I like this book.
* 这本书，我很喜欢。 — Zhè běn shū, wǒ hěn xǐhuan. — This book, I really like.

The fronted object can be interpreted as a topic already active or being contrasted in discourse. Topic and grammatical subject are not identical categories.

